---
import ExternalLink from '../components/ExternalLink.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/page.css';

const description =
  'Full-stack engineer drawn to inspectable agent systems: traces, latency, and cost, local-first.';
---

<BaseLayout title="Joseph Chow" description={description}>
  <main class="main">
    <section class="content">
      <p class="heading">Hello.</p>
      <h1 class="subheading">My name is Joseph Chow.</h1>
      <p class="text">
        Full-stack engineer. I'm drawn to the quiet parts of agent systems: the
        tool calls that usually vanish into a black box. I like building so you
        can actually see what's happening: traces, latency, and cost, on your
        own machine. Local-first, on purpose.
      </p>
      <p class="text">
        Lately that curiosity became
        <ExternalLink href="https://github.com/chowjiaming/toolcall-timeline"
          >toolcall-timeline</ExternalLink
        >: a local inspector for MCP tool calls, with waterfall timing,
        payloads, and session cost when the data is there.
      </p>
      <p class="text">
        I like small, sharp tools more than big platforms. If I can't look
        inside something, I'm slow to trust it. I'd rather ship a loop I can
        watch, then grow it carefully from there.
      </p>
      <p class="text">
        Away from the keyboard I'm in Toronto, studying Mandarin and Cantonese
        for family, Vietnamese for community, and French because I'm curious
        about it.
      </p>
      <p class="text">
        Reach me on
        <ExternalLink href="https://github.com/chowjiaming"
          >GitHub</ExternalLink
        >,
        <ExternalLink href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/chowjiaming/"
          >LinkedIn</ExternalLink
        >, or at
        <ExternalLink href="mailto:contact@josephchow.dev"
          >contact@josephchow.dev</ExternalLink
        >.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
